# Belligerent Yearling: "that creature's power" is read as the ability resolves (CR 608.2h), not as the Dinosaur entered - Bot1 casts the Yearling and a Giant
# Cindermaw (a 4/3 Dinosaur), and with the trigger on the stack casts Giant Growth on the Cindermaw. Bot1 accepts and the Yearling's base power becomes 7, not 4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Belligerent Yearling
Giant Cindermaw
Giant Growth
Mountain
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Belligerent Yearling.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Cindermaw.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Growth.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Giant Cindermaw)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Giant Cindermaw.Power = 7
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Belligerent Yearling.Power = 7
Bot1.Battlefield.Belligerent Yearling.Toughness = 2
